# Measured-scope manifest for the coverage gate.
#
# READ BY `scripts/coverage.sh`. Every path below is a file that gate currently
# MEASURES — the set llvm-cov reports after `IGNORE` has removed the excluded ones.
# The gate re-derives that set on every run and FAILS, naming the files, when it
# differs from this list.
#
# IT RECORDS WHAT IS MEASURED. IT DOES NOT DECIDE WHAT SHOULD BE.
# The policy — which files are out of scope and why — is `IGNORE` in
# `scripts/coverage.sh`, argued entry by entry beside the regex, and this file is
# not a second copy of it. It is never passed to llvm-cov: the gate COMPARES it,
# never APPLIES it, so deleting a line here cannot exclude a file from measurement,
# it can only make the next run fail and say so. That asymmetry is the whole design.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Every term in `IGNORE` names a directory depth
# (`codeview[/\\][a-z_]+\.rs` matches flat files directly under `codeview/` and
# nothing deeper), so introducing `codeview/paint/` makes seven view-bound files stop
# matching and silently enter the measured scope at 0%. The ratchet does fail — but it
# fails as "your change reduced coverage", so the reader goes hunting for untested code
# they just wrote, when the event was a change in WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. The
# `window/`  term's `tabs/`, `editbar/` and `navhistory/` alternatives are each scar
# tissue from exactly that, added after the fact; the comments warning about it did not
# prevent the third recurrence, which is the tell that a comment was the wrong
# instrument. This file makes the scope change fail in its own register, first and by
# name.
#
# It catches the other direction too, and that direction has also happened here: a
# commit once raised `FLOOR` in the same change that added `clipboard` to `IGNORE`, so
# the floor climbed by NARROWING the scope rather than by testing anything (found by QA,
# not by a gate — see the 2026-08-21 entry in `scripts/coverage.sh`). A file leaving this
# list is coverage surrendered, and it now has to be stated to land.
#
# UPDATING IT IS A DELIBERATE ACT, in the same commit as the layout change, exactly as
# raising `FLOOR` is. Decide which side each named file belongs on FIRST — test it, or
# extend `IGNORE` with the narrowest term that names it and its rationale — then record
# the decision with:
#
#     scripts/coverage.sh --update-scope
#
# FORMAT: one repo-relative, `/`-separated path per line, `LC_ALL=C` sorted; `#`
# comments and blank lines ignored. The separator is `/` even though llvm-cov reports
# native paths (`src\theme\decor.rs` on Windows) — the gate normalises before it
# compares, so this file is identical on every platform.
